  "title": "Stuttgart: combating the heat island effect and poor air quality with ventilation corridors and green-blue infrastructure",
  "summary": "Stuttgart, prone to air pollution and urban heat island effect, used a Climate Atlas to develop zoning regulations. Preserving open space, expanding green areas, and implementing measures like green roofs enhances resilience to heatwaves and improve urban air quality. Stuttgart’s location in a valley basin, its mild climate, low wind speeds, industrial activity and high volume of traffic has made the city highly susceptible to poor air quality. Development on the valley slopes has prevented air from moving through the city, worsening air quality and contributing to the urban heat island effect.",
